# Database (Prisma 6 + Neon)

- Always import the client as `import { db } from "@/lib/db"`. Never create new `PrismaClient` instances.
- `DATABASE_URL` is the pooled Neon URL; `DIRECT_URL` is the direct URL used for migrations.
- After editing `prisma/schema.prisma`, create a migration with `npm run db:migrate -- --name <change>`. Never edit an applied migration.
- Models:
  - `Filing`: pre-payment application (status DRAFT → AWAITING_PAYMENT → PAID).
  - `Order`: created only by the webhook. `orderNumber` is random (`generateOrderNumber`), `lsOrderId` is unique for idempotency.
  - `OrderEvent`: every status change on an `Order` must also create an `OrderEvent` (powers the tracking timeline).
- Use `$transaction` when updating `Filing` and creating `Order` together.
- Prefer adding nullable columns or defaults so existing rows stay valid.
